00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:32.860
Option spreads can turn a single contract directional trade into a lower cost structure by selling a second contract against the first.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:42.480
Today's market shows how this approach defines risk upfront while still capturing the core thesis, though it caps upside if the move exceeds the short strike.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:53.160
A listener holding one long call on a rebounding name could sell an out-of-the-money call at the same expiration to reduce net debit and create a defined risk debit spread.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:05.920
The trade-off appears clearly in back-tested one-contract examples, where the spread lowered entry cost by roughly 30% to 40% on average, but limited gains once the underlying moved beyond the short leg.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:12.380
This mechanic works best when volatility is elevated enough to inflate the credit received on the short side.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:18.100
Risk rises if the spread is held through binary events that produce gap moves beyond the strikes.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:27.000
Disclaimer, this is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. No real money is involved. This is not financial advice.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:36.700
Today's practice investment is a flash trade on hps.a. Hammond Power Solutions listed on the TSX in the industrial sector.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:45.760
The approach uses a valuation entry on pullback into data center infrastructure spending with a five session hold and an 8% stop.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:55.020
The catalyst is accelerating Canadian data center build out demand for electrical equipment, with the name already trading at a discount to recent highs.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:03.000
Price pulled back from 52 week highs with volume near the 20-day average and nearest support at the 50-day moving average.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.420
The stop limits loss on the $1,000 position to roughly $80.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:14.060
The target is 4-8% over the five session window if the infrastructure spending narrative holds.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:22.780
This is a medium confidence setup because the fundamental spending trend is visible, but volume confirmation remains average rather than elevated.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:31.480
The invalidation line is clear. The thesis fails if quarterly revenue guidance from data center customers falls below the prior quarter's run rate.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:39.940
This setup demonstrates how to screen for names already discounted after sector rotation yet still tied to a multi-year spending cycle.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:51.960
Yesterday's flash trade on gmyn.to entered at $54.47 on the Tuesday open and exited at $56.33 at the close.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:59.360
The position gained 3.41% or $34.15 on the $1,000 allocation.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:05.800
The same day exit captured the immediate reaction without giving the position time to reverse on profit taking.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:14.620
That outcome aligns with the rule requiring volume above the 20-day average before entering any catalyst driven name already in a sector rotation.

